IMPORT prelude

-- Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore Act 2022 (Singapore) -- what "gambling" means for the Authority (s 2), the offence of
-- misusing the Authority's symbol (s 8), who may sit on the Authority and how long, and when a seat is lost (ss 11, 16, 18, 20),
-- quorum and resolutions (ss 23, 25), the secrecy offence for insiders (s 34), the shield from personal liability (s 35), compounding
-- (s 43), liability of officers of a corporation (s 44), and service of documents (s 46).
--
-- Edition: Act 14 of 2022, informal consolidation ("version in force from 30/10/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/GRASA2022.txt. The only amendment annotated in the deposit is Act 29 of 2024 (wef 30/10/2024),
-- to s 5(1)(d) and (5). The deposit carries no legislative history table.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. REQ-0148 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. This is an institutional Act: it continues the Casino Regulatory Authority as the Gambling Regulatory Authority and
-- sets up its constitution. The licensing of gambling itself is in the Gambling Control Act 2022 and the Casino Control Act 2006, not
-- here. SCOPED to the provisions a member of the public, a business, a would-be member or an insider actually meets. Not encoded: the
-- functions and powers (ss 5-6) beyond the s 2 definition, Ministerial directions (s 7), appointment mechanics other than term and
-- resignation (ss 9, 10, 12-15, 17), presiding and execution of documents (ss 24, 26), committees and delegation (ss 27-30),
-- personnel and finance (ss 31-33, 36-42), offences by unincorporated associations (s 45, which mirrors s 44), regulations (s 47), the
-- amendments to other Acts (Part 8) and the savings (Part 9).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore Act 2022`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 -- gambling`

-- s 2: "gambling" INCLUDES any of the following "which is not social gambling": (a) participating in a lottery; (b) playing a game of
-- chance "(which includes a game that is partly a game of chance and partly a game requiring skill)"; (c) making or accepting bets or
-- bookmaking. "social gambling" has the meaning given by the Gambling Control Act 2022 (not read for this row).
-- The definition is inclusive, so FALSE below means only that none of (a) to (c) names the activity, not that it can never be gambling.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `buying a lottery ticket`
    `playing a slot machine`
    `playing a card game that mixes chance and skill`
    `placing a bet on a football match`
    `taking bets as a bookmaker`
    `playing a game of pure skill for a prize`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `it is social gambling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is one of the listed kinds of gambling` IF
        (NOT `it is social gambling`)
    AND CONSIDER `the activity`
        WHEN `playing a game of pure skill for a prize` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8 -- the Authority's symbol`

-- s 8(2): a person who "(a) uses, without the prior written permission of the Authority, a symbol or representation identical with the
-- Authority's symbol or representation; or (b) uses a symbol or representation which so resembles the Authority's symbol or
-- representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" is guilty of an offence: "a fine
-- not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- On its words, the permission exception appears only in (a). Read literally, a confusingly similar symbol is an offence even with
-- permission. (That is the text; whether a court would read the permission into (b) is not decided here.)
GIVEN `uses an identical symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Authority's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a confusingly similar symbol` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `misusing the Authority's symbol is an offence` IF
        (`uses an identical symbol` AND (NOT `had the Authority's prior written permission`))
    OR  `uses a confusingly similar symbol`

GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for misusing the symbol` MEANS 10000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

§§ `11 -- who is disqualified from membership`

-- s 11(2): disqualified are (a) "an undischarged bankrupt or an individual who has an arrangement with any of his or her creditors";
-- (b) "a Judge or judicial officer"; (c) "an individual who has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more, and has
-- not received a free pardon"; (d) a person disqualified as a company director under s 154(1), or by court order under s 149(1),
-- 149A(1) or 154(2), of the Companies Act 1967, during the disqualification; (e) an individual who lacks capacity for the duties within
-- the Mental Capacity Act 2008, or is subject to an order under s 10 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008.
-- s 14(3): the same disqualifications bar an acting appointment.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `undischarged bankrupt or in an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `longest single prison sentence in months` IS A NUMBER
    `has a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disqualified as a company director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lacks capacity or is under a mental health order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified from membership` IF
        `the candidate`'s `undischarged bankrupt or in an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `longest single prison sentence in months` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `has a free pardon`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `disqualified as a company director`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `lacks capacity or is under a mental health order`

§§ `16, 18 and 20 -- term, resignation and losing the seat`

-- s 18(1): "each member of the Authority holds office for a period of 3 years or any shorter period specified in the instrument of
-- appointment"; (2) re-appointment is allowed. Here 0 means the instrument specifies no period. A specified period LONGER than 3 years
-- is read as 3 (an inference: the text allows only "3 years or any shorter period").
GIVEN `years specified in the instrument` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of office in years` MEANS
    IF `years specified in the instrument` GREATER THAN 0 AND `years specified in the instrument` LESS THAN 3
    THEN `years specified in the instrument`
    ELSE 3

-- s 16(2): a resignation "is effective when the notice ... is received by the Minister or at any later time specified in the notice".
-- Days are counted as day numbers; a specified day earlier than receipt has no effect (the text allows only "any later time").
GIVEN `day the Minister received the notice` IS A NUMBER, `day specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the resignation takes effect` MEANS
    IF `day specified in the notice` GREATER THAN `day the Minister received the notice`
    THEN `day specified in the notice`
    ELSE `day the Minister received the notice`

-- s 20(1)(g): a member ceases to hold office if he or she "fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Authority without the approval
-- of the Authority". (Other grounds: death, bankruptcy, disqualification, removal, resignation, undisclosed interest, no re-appointment.)
-- s 20(2): no compensation on ceasing to hold office "for any reason".
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `the Authority approved the absences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member loses the seat for absence` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `the Authority approved the absences`)

§§ `23 and 25 -- quorum and resolutions`

-- s 23(1): "The quorum is the number that is one-third the number of members or 3 members, whichever is higher." (2) "No business may
-- be transacted at a meeting of the Authority if a quorum is not present."
-- The text does not say how a fraction is rounded. The encoding requires at least one-third: with 10 members, 3 present is 9/30 short
-- of one-third, so 4 are needed (an inference). s 9(1): the Authority has 5 to 17 members.
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `number of members` AND `members present` AT LEAST 3

-- s 25(1) one vote each; (2) the presiding member has a casting vote "in the case of an equality of votes"; (3) a resolution "is passed
-- if it is agreed by all members present without dissent, or if a majority of the members who are entitled to vote on the matter cast
-- votes in favour of it"; (4) a member present "is presumed to have agreed to, and to have voted in favour of" a resolution "unless he or
-- she expressly dissents from or votes against" it.
-- Because of (4), silence is a vote in favour: votes for = those present and entitled minus those who dissent. "A majority of the
-- members who are entitled to vote" is read as a majority of those present and entitled (an inference; it could mean all members
-- entitled, present or not).
GIVEN `present and entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER, `expressly dissenting or voting against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote in favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resolution is passed` IF
        `expressly dissenting or voting against` EQUALS 0
    OR  (`present and entitled to vote` MINUS `expressly dissenting or voting against`) TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `present and entitled to vote`
    OR  ((`present and entitled to vote` MINUS `expressly dissenting or voting against`) TIMES 2 EQUALS `present and entitled to vote` AND `casting vote in favour`)

§§ `34 -- secrecy`

-- s 34(1): a member, employee, delegate or subdelegate, the Chief Executive or a committee member "who has information in his or her
-- capacity as such that would not otherwise be available to him or her, must not disclose that information to any person except" --
-- (a) in performing the Authority's functions; (b) "with the prior authorisation from the Authority"; (c) for proceedings for an
-- offence under this Act or a report of them; (d) "as required by an order of court"; (e) in complying with the duty to disclose
-- interests; (f) as required or allowed by or under this Act or any other Act.
-- (2): "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both".
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `in performing the Authority's functions`
    `with the Authority's prior authorisation`
    `for proceedings for an offence under this Act`
    `under a court order`
    `in disclosing an interest as the Act requires`
    `as another Act requires or allows`
    `to a friend over dinner`
    `to a journalist`

GIVEN `is an insider of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the information came through the role` IS A BOOLEAN, `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is a secrecy offence` IF
        `is an insider of the Authority`
    AND `the information came through the role`
    AND CONSIDER `the disclosure`
        WHEN `to a friend over dinner` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to a journalist` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

`the maximum fine for a secrecy offence` MEANS 2000
`the maximum imprisonment in months for a secrecy offence` MEANS 24

§§ `35 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 35: "No liability shall lie against" a member, committee member, the Chief Executive, an employee, delegate or subdelegate, "or any
-- other person acting under the direction of the Authority", for anything done or omitted "in good faith AND with reasonable care" in
-- performing the Authority's functions or exercising its powers. Good faith alone is not enough.
GIVEN `acting for the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is shielded from personal liability` IF
    `acting for the Authority` AND `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care`

§§ `43 -- composition of offences`

-- s 43(1): the Chief Executive or an authorised employee "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable
-- offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000." (2) on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken". (3) the sums go to the
-- Consolidated Fund. Which offences are prescribed was not read (no regulations retrieved).
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded` IF `prescribed as compoundable`

GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS `the lower of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `44 -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 44(2): where a corporation commits an offence under this Act, a person who is "(i) an officer of the corporation; or (ii) an
-- individual involved in the management of the corporation and in a position to influence the conduct of the corporation" AND who
-- "(i) consented or connived, or conspired with others", "(ii) is ... knowingly concerned in, or is party to," the offence, or "(iii) knew
-- or ought reasonably to have known that the offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to take all reasonable steps to
-- prevent or stop" it, "shall be guilty of that same offence". (3) the person may rely on the corporation's defences, with the same
-- burden. (5) this "applies whether or not the corporation is convicted". "corporation" includes a limited liability partnership.
GIVEN `the corporation committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a manager able to influence the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knowingly concerned or party to it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or ought reasonably to have known` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps to prevent or stop it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of the corporation's offence` IF
        `the corporation committed the offence`
    AND (`an officer` OR `a manager able to influence the conduct`)
    AND (    `consented, connived or conspired`
         OR  `knowingly concerned or party to it`
         OR  (`knew or ought reasonably to have known` AND (NOT `took all reasonable steps to prevent or stop it`)))

§§ `46 -- service of documents on an individual`

-- s 46(2): an individual may be served (a) personally; (b) by prepaid registered post; (c) by leaving it with an adult at home or at
-- work; (d) by affixing a copy "in a conspicuous place" at the residential or business address; (e) by fax; (f) by email to the last
-- email address. (5) "In addition, a document (other than a summons)" may be served by an electronic notice at the chosen means of
-- notification. (7) service by email or by electronic notice "may be effected only with the person's prior consent (express or
-- implied)". (8) the section does not apply to documents in court proceedings.
-- (6)(c): by post, service takes effect "2 days after the day the document was posted (even if it is returned undelivered)".
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `personal delivery`
    `registered post`
    `leaving it with an adult at home`
    `affixing it at the address`
    `fax`
    `email`
    `electronic notice`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method, `the individual consented to electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the document is a summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method may be used to serve the individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `email` THEN `the individual consented to electronic service`
    WHEN `electronic notice` THEN `the individual consented to electronic service` AND (NOT `the document is a summons`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `day posted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day service by post takes effect` MEANS `day posted` PLUS 2
